card.statement:
Isomorphism classes of commutative algebras $A$ in the braided category $\cC(\h,\Omega)$, which have a non-degenerate multiplicative bilinear form and have trivial subalgebra of invariants $A^\h=k$, are in one to one correspondence with subgroups $\gl\subset\h$ such that the restriction of the form on $\gl$ is integer and even

\begin{equation}
(x,y)\in\Z,\quad (x,x)\in 2\Z,\quad x,y\in\gl.
\end{equation}
